# pseudocode source: chapters/ch52.tex:63
# caption: Validate the progress assumptions of the backtracking generator.

REQUIRE parsed grammar with ordered alternatives and terminal regex trees
ENSURE valid symbols and no recursive call cycle before input consumption
require one defined start; reject unknown directives and undefined symbols
reject every terminal or layout expression that may accept epsilon
compute nullable nonterminals by production fixed-point iteration
initialize an empty left-corner graph
FORALL productions A -> X_1... X_k DO
  FOR j=1,...,k DO
    IF X_j is a terminal THEN
      BREAK
    END IF
    add edge A -> X_j
    IF X_j is not nullable THEN
      BREAK
    END IF
  END FOR
END FOR
reject if a depth-first traversal finds a gray-to-gray edge
check RHS sizes, regex expansion limits, and action references

